    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n32490" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ŏlĭtōrĭus</span></b>  (or,
		better, <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">hŏlĭtōrĭus</span></b> ),
			a, um, adj.
		olitor, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>of</i> or <i>belonging to a
				kitchengardener</i> or <i>to vegetables</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">forum olitorium erat antiquum, macellum, ubi
					olerum copia,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Varr. L. L. 5, § 146</span></i>
			 Müll.; so, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">forum,</span>”
				<i>the green-market</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Liv.
					21, 62</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ostiola,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					19, 8, 38, § 125</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">rotae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					19, 5, 23, § 64</span></i>
			 Sillig <i>N. cr.</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">horti,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Dig. 50, 16, 198</span></i>
			.</div>
